CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261020T141736Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u>AOS: 16:23:39 UTC<br>RX:<b> 145.800 MHz </b>- FM over US
 A<br><br><b>School Information: <br></b>The Sarasota Military Academy\, fou
 nded in 2002\, is a tuition-free\, nonprofit\, military public charter scho
 ol located in Sarasota\, Florida. Our goal in our community is to equip our
  cadets with the skills\, values\, and education that will enable them to l
 ead productive and fulfilling lives. The Sarasota Military Academy is a one
 -cost-center educational institution with two campuses\, serving middle sch
 ool (grades 6-8) and high school (grades 9-12) students at each campus resp
 ectively. All of our high school students are enrolled in the United States
  Army’s JROTC (Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps) curriculum\, and both
  campuses have strict student uniform and behavior standards.<br>In 2009\, 
 at the request of founding headmaster Dan Kennedy\, George Becht N2SQ began
  W4SMA\, our on-campus radio club. The club entered a period of suspended a
 nimation in 2014\, and was rebooted by George Becht and John Geimer K4GEI i
 n the spring of 2024. W4SMA now offers students the ability to take a scien
 ce elective course focused on Radio\, Wireless Communications\, and Electro
 nics and facilitates on-campus amateur radio testing. More than 30 cadets h
 ave obtained their licenses\, and some have upgraded to General and Amateur
  Extra. W4SMA strives to equip our students with the knowledge and skills n
 ecessary to participate in the world of radio\, and to integrate that knowl
 edge with whatever paths through life they choose.<br><br><b>Students First
  Names &amp\; Questions:<br></b>1. In your opinion\, do you think military 
 technologies have generally improved international relations in space?<br>2
 . How did looking down at Earth change the way you view everyday problems b
 ack home?<br>3. Do you think commercial public space travel is realistic wi
 thin the next 20 years for anyone other than the ultra-wealthy?<br>4. Are t
 here benefits or drawbacks to fielding astronauts with a purely civilian ba
 ckground?<br>5. Do you think there will be another chance for international
  cooperation in space after the ISS is retired?<br>6. How have experiments 
 conducted on the Space Station influenced the lives of regular people in wa
 ys they might not be aware of?<br>7. What would you consider a “very bad” d
 ay on ISS?<br>8. How similar is the method of creating oxygen on a spacecra
 ft to that of a submarine?<br>9. What are the most interesting physics demo
 nstrations or experiments on the ISS that would have behaved differently if
  conducted on Earth?<br>10. Do auroras look different in space than they do
  on Earth?<br>11. In your opinion\, do you believe that modern technology h
 as reached the point that it has practically plateaued?<br>12. How much has
  the ISS contributed to advancing humans toward a higher class of civilizat
 ion?<br>13. How do solar storms affect experiments on the ISS\, and what ha
 ppens if something requires you redo an experiment?<br>14. How have experim
 ents onboard the Space Station affected the sciences and technologies of pr
 opulsion?<br>15. What is the most unexpected skill you have found yourself 
 having to use during your time on the Space Station?<br>16. If you’re able 
 to share\, what experiments are you currently working on?<br>17. How danger
 ous are solar storms to the astronauts inside the ISS?
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T141737Z
LOCATION:Sarasota Military Academy\, 801 N Orange Ave\, Sarasota\, FL 34236
 \, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:NA1SS (Luke Delaney KJ5PPF) - 24 deg - W4SMA ( Sarasota\, FL)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
