CREATED:20190603T194038Z
DESCRIPTION:AOS:&nbsp\;18:11:51 UTC  <br>RX:<b> 145.800 MHz </b>- FM over U
 SA<br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>School Information:&nbsp\;</b><br>National Air a
 nd Space Museum – Steven F. Udvar-Hazy Center<br>Innovations in Flight Fami
 ly Day<br>The theme of this program is to give museum visitors the opportun
 ity to learn about the innovations in aircraft design and what it takes to 
 become a pilot by talking with pilots about how they learned to fly\, what 
 they fly\, and how they use their aircraft.  The day is designed to inform 
 visitors of the opportunities in both military and civilian aviation.  Visi
 tors have the opportunity to talk with a diversified group of pilots to see
  different types of aircraft.  This year we are celebrating the 50th Annive
 rsary of the Apollo Program.<br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><b>Students First Names &
 amp\; Questions:</b><br>1. Isaiah:  What is your favorite thing to do in mi
 crogravity? <br>2. Joel:  How important are the people in mission control?&
 nbsp\;<br>3. Natalia:  What is a normal day look like?&nbsp\;<br>4. Sonja: 
  What was the launch like?&nbsp\;<br>5. Alejandro:  What is your least favo
 rite part of being in space?&nbsp\;<br>6. Sam:  Are there any animals on st
 ation?&nbsp\;<br>7. Joshua:  Did you know you wanted to be an astronaut whe
 n you were a kid?&nbsp\;<br>8. Jake:  There is a NASA T-38 at this event\, 
 what was your biggest challenge in learning to fly?&nbsp\;<br>9. Bryce:  Wh
 ere are you now?&nbsp\;<br>10. Isaiah:  What is your favorite space food?&n
 bsp\;<br>11. Joel:  What happens if someone gets sick?&nbsp\;<br>12. Natali
 a:  What is around you?&nbsp\;<br>13. Sonja:  Do you have a degree in scien
 ce?&nbsp\;<br>14. Alejandro:  What kind of exercise do you do?&nbsp\;<br>15
 . Sam:  Do you have ice cream?&nbsp\;<br>16. Joshua:  Do you ever get bored
 ?&nbsp\;<br>17. Jake:  What did you take up with you that is special?&nbsp\
 ;<br>18. Bryce:  What do you miss?&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260417T040354Z
LOCATION:Smithsonian Air and Space – Udvar-Hazy\, Chantilly\, VA\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:NA1SS (Nick Hague KG5TMV) - 42 deg - (TB) W6SRJ (Chantilly\, VA)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
